      "id": "nm000284",
      "name": "STRUM: Small Team Reconnaissance Urban Missions",
      "description": "STRUM is a dyadic neuroergonomics dataset recording pairs of participants performing a collaborative urban-reconnaissance task, with simultaneous multimodal physiological and behavioral recordings from both team members via Lab Streaming Layer. The dataset includes EEG, EMG, ECG/EOG, motion capture, eye-tracking, force plate, and behavioral/event data across 33 sessions (66 participants), converted to BIDS format with dyad pairing encoded via participant metadata rather than hierarchy.",
