    {
      "dataset_id": "on003490",
      "id": "on003490",
      "name": "EEG: 3-Stim Auditory Oddball and Rest in Parkinson's",
      "description": "This dataset contains resting-state and 3-stimulus auditory oddball EEG recordings from 25 Parkinson's disease patients and 25 matched healthy controls, collected circa 2015 at the Cognitive Rhythms and Computation Lab, University of New Mexico. Parkinson's patients were assessed twice, one week apart, either ON or OFF dopaminergic medication, while controls were tested once. Accelerometer data (X, Y, Z axes) were also recorded from participants' most tremor-affected hand, alongside eyes-open/eyes-closed resting segments.",
